{"title":"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 29","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of the following could NOT be the lengths of the external diagonals of a right regular prism [a \"box\"]? (An <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e65587a66ad30dfa84c8ce3ab465aa5ae68f4543.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{external diagonal}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"125\" height=\"15\" /> is a diagonal of one of the rectangular faces of the box.)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/a/5fad6ccfa4958b764c9731cc96af07d19c739f50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) }\\{4,5,6\\} \\quad \\text{(B) } \\{4,5,7\\}  \\quad \\text{(C) } \\{4,6,7\\} \\quad \\text{(D) } \\{5,6,7\\} \\quad \\text{(E) } \\{5,7,8\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"525\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/8/7c8acfd7d5ee559262593701b8dbd02e43ad96e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"13\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/1/5b1d6265e67657b5886ce257671d45ff9c0282eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"12\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the side lengths of the rectangular prism. By Pythagoras, the lengths of the external diagonals are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/6/746e0cd4f0edb108cdc654282e0704c8db1fb4a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{a^2 + b^2},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"20\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/6/366adb26bd8d6843a05552c40d9f30fcf376b815.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{b^2 + c^2},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/e/eae1d21769d41229d7a6cba0a6a0e67e578d4c76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{a^2 + c^2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> If we square each of these to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/1/ab1940ba0a8b46a28111585cbf34cfa57ff38038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + b^2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"20\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/a/a1a37925f54101feaaa5ba55b5269cad2ccbf8f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2 + c^2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/7/8972c2096b379ce3952fc1f808719da4218043a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + c^2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> we observe that since each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/8/7c8acfd7d5ee559262593701b8dbd02e43ad96e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"13\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/1/5b1d6265e67657b5886ce257671d45ff9c0282eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"12\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are positive, then the sum of any two of the squared diagonal lengths must be larger than the square of the third diagonal length. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/b/02b3867a2cf99e40a02d3c199a788b3a62001b51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a^2 + b^2) + (b^2 + c^2) = (a^2 + c^2) + 2b^2 &gt; a^2 + c^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"375\" height=\"19\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/a/05ab03d05eec058182bda044da89184aaed17177.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2b^2 &gt; 0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Thus, we test each answer choice to see if the sum of the squares of the two smaller numbers is larger than the square of the largest number. Looking at choice (B), we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/5/0f524993398200c4c9c583f3b187aec89dcd1aa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^2 + 5^2 = 41 &lt; 7^2 = 49,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"184\" height=\"18\" /> so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/1/d912533b82b38cae169f014c29a2f69537f6fe90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(B) \\{4, 5, 7\\}}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"107\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>--goldentail141\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/8/7c8acfd7d5ee559262593701b8dbd02e43ad96e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"13\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/1/5b1d6265e67657b5886ce257671d45ff9c0282eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"12\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the side lengths of the rectangular prism. We then have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/a/3aa311e429e68af9070d75b6a72b74776f54b7ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2=i^2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/e/20e53eeacdcceeed1ec2726651806100612d423f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2+c^2=j^2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/3/2b3ccd457ddc4552b965b14cbbaca02368cba075.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c^2+a^2=k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/c/27c58e97b5b4ffd5d9d28b608ff2fb9400546773.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{ i,j,k \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> are the given diagonal lengths. WLOG, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/c/75ccc80f047196808826a5f0a5153ea67c287a64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\leq j \\leq k.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" /> It suffices to check if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/6/2c69928c10ba896dac938ed04303405526b18680.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i^2+j^2 \\geq k.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" /> We see that for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2e33ab9a00e021af49e888212645d4667903c49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/1/251b550b737a9e27a377570e429850342aecdf4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^2+5^2 = 16 + 25 = 41 &lt; 7^2 = 49$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"266\" height=\"18\" />, so this case is impossible.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME\" title=\"1993 AHSME\">1993 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1993 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1993\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">Problem 28</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 30\">Problem 30</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 25\">25</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">26</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">27</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">28</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">29</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 30\">30</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AHSME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AHSME Problems and Solutions\"> All AHSME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017183649\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.059 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 216/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2494/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 152/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5446/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.127      1 -total\n 57.44%    6.966      1 Template:AHSME_box\n 40.08%    4.860      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:12916:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017183649 and revision id 175674. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}